                <head>220. Editorial Note</head>
                <p>On October 7, the U.N. Security Council voted
                    unanimously to recommend to the General Assembly that the Federation of Nigeria
                    be admitted to the United Nations. Secretary of State Herter gave the U.S.
                    statement endorsing this proposal; for text of his statement and a record of
                    these proceedings, see U.N. doc. S/PV.908.</p>
                <p>That afternoon the General Assembly decided by acclamation to grant Nigeria
                        U.N. membership. Assistant Secretary of State
                    for International Organization Affairs Wilcox gave the U.S. statement welcoming Nigeria to the United
                    Nations; for text of his statement and a record of these proceedings, see U.N.
                    doc. A/PV.893. For text of the resolution
                    admitting Nigeria to the United Nations, see U.N. General Assembly Resolution
                    1492 (XV), printed in U.N. doc. A4684.</p>
            </div>
